  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen UNICEF WEP-WASH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&apos;s main objective is to evaluate the viability of wind energy as a sustainable power source for water supply facilities in Yemen. If wind energy proves feasible for this purpose, the project aims to identify and recommend wind energy solutions that are well-suited to the unique needs and circumstances of Yemen.The scope of work and required expertise would involve:-	Assessing wind resources in Yemen (for water supply systems), wind and energy profiles;-	Assessing technologies for (small and large) scale wind energy production;-	Energy consumption profiles for water supply systems (rural, peri-urban, urban);-	Evaluate the technical feasibility of wind energy for water supply;-	Describe (on a conceptual level) how typical wind energy-water supply systems would look and operate.The project consists of three parts. In each part, there will be a knowledge session which has a two-fold objective: 1)	Yemeni validation of results and 2)	transfer of knowledge.</narrative>
  </description>
